      "id": "foqv3i9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Volcanoes"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Volcanoes are broadly classified based on eruptive activity (active, dormant, extinct) and structural shape.",
        "Earthquakes release accumulated tectonic stress, radiating energy outward via body waves and surface waves.",
        "Seismic waves are categorized into primary (P) waves, secondary (S) waves, and surface (L) waves.",
        "Earthquake magnitude is measured logarithmically on the Richter scale, while damage intensity is assessed using the Mercalli scale.",
        "The majority of global volcanic eruptions and seismic shocks occur along the Circum-Pacific Belt."
      ],
      "id": "8iaqdfx"
    },
