    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "P-waves are compressional waves that travel through solids, liquids, and gases, whereas S-waves are shear waves that travel only through solids.",
        "The Richter Scale measures energy released (magnitude), while the Mercalli Scale measures visible destruction and impact (intensity).",
        "The Circum-Pacific Belt (Pacific Ring of Fire) accounts for nearly 68% of the world's earthquakes."
      ],
